{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.add_comment` is the only `--json` consumer in that module that\nreturns raw `json.loads(result.stdout)` straight to its caller\n(`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py:549-550`). Every sibling\nnormalizes or verifies the payload first: `get_comments` -> `_parse_paginated_comments`,\n`_parse_acli_comments` (normalizes bare list / wrapped dict / unrecognised shape), `get_issue`\n(unwraps `issues[0]`, raises when absent), `create_issue` -> `_verify_created_issue` (raises\nloudly when no key, `acli_cli_ops.py:40`).\n\nBecause `add_comment` skips that idiom, it hands its caller ACLI's batch mutation envelope\n(`{\"results\": [...], \"totalCount\": N, \"successCount\": N}`) while its declared type\n(`_backend.py:585`: `add_comment(...) -> dict[str, Any]`) and its consumer\n(`dispatch_apply_phases._record_comment_id`, which reads `result.get(\"id\")`) treat it as a\ncreated comment resource. That gap is exactly what let bug `irongrey-chubby-oxpecker`\n(`aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615`) ship: `_record_comment_id` read `result[\"id\"]`, got `None` on every\nCloud post, and silently no-opped — re-posting ~205 comments an hour until REB-1861 hit Jira's\n5000-comment cap. The aa7b fix made `_record_comment_id` tolerant (records\n`UNKNOWN_COMMENT_ID` when no id), but the transport boundary itself still returns the\nsemantically-wrong shape, and `results[].id` (the WORK ITEM key) remains a trap for any future\nconsumer.\n\n## Approach\n\nNormalize at the transport boundary, mirroring the sibling idiom:\n\n1. Add a module-level helper `_parse_comment_created(stdout: str) -> dict[str, Any]` in\n   `acli_cli_ops.py`, called by `add_comment` in place of raw `json.loads`:\n   - A dict WITHOUT the batch-envelope markers (`results` / `successCount`) is a comment\n     resource (the DC/REST-shaped `{\"id\": \"10001\"}` that\n     `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_comment_adf_encode.py:52` pins) — returned\n     verbatim. Assume any non-envelope dict is a resource (default; no shape allowlist).\n   - The batch envelope is returned as an honest comment-resource-shaped dict\n     `{\"id\": None, \"acli_envelope\": <parsed>}`: explicit `id: None` because ACLI echoes no\n     comment id, envelope preserved under a clearly-named key so `results[].id` (the WORK\n     ITEM key, not a comment id) can never be mistaken for one. FAILURE envelopes never reach\n     the normalizer: `acli_subprocess._run_acli` already raises `AcliMutationError` via\n     `_check_mutation_failure` (`acli_subprocess.py:299-345`, bug 44de).\n   - Any other shape (bare list, scalar, non-JSON handled by json.loads raising) raises\n     `RuntimeError` naming the payload, mirroring `_verify_created_issue`'s loud failure.\n2. Update the `acli_result` fixture assertions in\n   `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py` (which currently pin\n   the raw-envelope passthrough) to the normalized contract; its four dedup tests must keep\n   passing unchanged (the recording path still stores `UNKNOWN_COMMENT_ID`).\n3. Commit a RECORDED real ACLI comment-create payload: the failure envelope captured live\n   today against acli 1.3.19 via the safe probe\n   `acli jira workitem comment create --key NONEXIST-999999 --json` (exit=0,\n   `successCount: 0`, `results[0].id == \"NONEXIST-999999\"` — no mutation performed). Embed it\n   as a constant with a provenance note and assert `_check_mutation_failure` raises\n   `AcliMutationError` on it, plus normalizer unit tests against the already-recorded SUCCESS\n   envelope (verified live against acli 1.3.19 by fix 8d98c298fa8).\n4. Audit the remaining `--json` mutation wrappers for raw passthrough —\n   `acli_cli_ops.create_issue` paths (`_create_issue_no_json`, `_create_from_json_payload`),\n   `update_priority` (REST, no JSON return), `get_issue`, `get_comments`, and the\n   module-level `acli.update_issue` (`acli.py:211` returns `json.loads(result.stdout)` raw\n   for `workitem edit`) — and record the findings as a comment on this ticket; file a\n   `discovered_from` ticket for any consumer-reachable hazard found.\n5. Touch up the `_record_comment_id` docstring (`dispatch_apply_phases.py:311`) so its\n   description of the Cloud transport's return matches the normalized shape.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py` — add\n  `_parse_comment_created`; `add_comment` routes through it.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py` — update fixture\n  assertions to the normalized contract; add recorded failure-envelope constant + tests.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py` — docstring-only update to\n  `_record_comment_id`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: the recorded SUCCESS envelope driven through the real\n  `acli_cli_ops.add_comment` (stubbed at the `_run_acli` seam, as the existing fixture does)\n  returns `{\"id\": None, \"acli_envelope\": <envelope>}`; the DC/REST-shaped `{\"id\": \"10001\"}`\n  passes through verbatim (existing `test_acli_comment_adf_encode.py` assertion keeps\n  passing).\n- Failure/edge: the RECORDED failure envelope raises `AcliMutationError` in\n  `_check_mutation_failure`; a bare-list payload makes `_parse_comment_created` raise\n  `RuntimeError`.\n- Regression: all four existing dedup tests in `test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py` pass with\n  the normalized fixture (recording stores `UNKNOWN_COMMENT_ID`; re-diff emits nothing).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `add_comment` no longer returns the raw batch envelope: SUCCESS envelope ->\n      `{\"id\": None, \"acli_envelope\": ...}`, resource-shaped payload -> verbatim, unrecognized\n      shape -> `RuntimeError` — checked by\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_comment_adf_encode.py`.\n- [ ] At least one test asserts against a RECORDED real ACLI comment-create payload (the\n      live-captured failure envelope with its provenance note) rather than an invented one —\n      checked by reading the committed constant's provenance comment and running its test.\n- [ ] The remaining `acli_cli_ops` `--json` mutation wrappers (and `acli.update_issue`) are\n      audited for raw passthrough and the finding is recorded as a comment on this ticket —\n      checked by the comment's presence on the ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787443320525418001,"uuid":"51bca6af-9185-448a-88c4-f818710e987e"}